  "findings": [
    "All four stock-cloud commands were accepted by the same associated chassis, and only one port was active in each payload.",
    "The branch-6 command port is packed across offsets 16 and 17: zone = 2 * (frame[16] & 0x7f) + ((frame[17] >> 7) & 1), while frame[17] & 0x7f remains 1.",
    "Offset 15 is 0x82 for open and 0x81 for close; offset 14 remains the already validated 0x90 open and 0x10 close operation marker.",
    "The branch-6 packing differs from the locally enrolled selector-2 command layout, so command construction must be association-profile-specific.",
    "Stock commands used both supported trailer residues without a fixed open/close mapping; the trailer must remain part of authenticated association state rather than be inferred from the requested operation.",
    "Open sequence values were 1, 2, 3, and 4; close sequence values were 2, 3, 4, and 5. A later repeated Zone 1 close used sequence 6, ruling out a fixed per-zone sequence but not yet identifying the stock gateway's advancement rule.",
    "The cloud application payload retained the requested 60-second session duration on the first stopped update, then cleared it on a later idle refresh.",
    "Battery remained 100 percent while RSSI varied per report, confirming that cloud RSSI is measured dynamically by the stock gateway."
  ]
